# Caseworker journeys

Journey boards for TEC caseworker review work. Frames reuse [TEC PCN blockframes](/tec-pcn-blockframes.html) and [ExUI form elements](/exui-form-elements.html). Yellow outline (`highlight`) and link-blue (`callout`) mark the control that starts each step. Hover blocks for element names.

## Journey: Enter a general application

The clerk is already on the **Case details** tab of a TEC PCN case, in any case state. They choose **Enter a general application** from the **Next step** dropdown and select **Go**. The illustrated path is an adjournment made without notice, where the parties do not consent, so every page is shown. Hearing date is skipped unless the type is Adjourn. The refer-to-judge page is skipped unless the parties do not consent and the application is without notice. Something else adds a categories text area on Application details.

How the event is stored is described in the tech docs: [Enter a general application](http://localhost:4568/enter-general-application.html).

<div class="bf-journey">
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_case_details", locals: { caption: "1. TEC PCN — Case details", highlight_tab: :case_details, highlight_next_step: true, next_step_event: "Enter a general application" } %><p class="bf-journey__note">On the <strong>Case details</strong> tab they open <strong>Next step</strong>, choose <strong>Enter a general application</strong>, and select <strong>Go</strong>.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Go</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_enter_general_application", locals: { caption: "2. Application details", page: :details } %><p class="bf-journey__note">They record who applied, a received date in the past, and the type. <strong>Something else</strong> also asks which categories apply.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Continue</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_enter_general_application", locals: { caption: "3. Hearing date", page: :hearing } %><p class="bf-journey__note">Shown only for <strong>Adjourn</strong>. They say whether a hearing is due in the next 14 days. This page does not change a hearing.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Continue</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_enter_general_application", locals: { caption: "4. Application fee", page: :fee } %><p class="bf-journey__note">They can continue only when the fee has already been received, and then enter the amount. <strong>No</strong> tells them to request payment first. Help with Fees asks for the reference when the answer is <strong>Yes</strong>.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Continue</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_enter_general_application", locals: { caption: "5. Consent and notice", page: :consent } %><p class="bf-journey__note">They say whether all parties consent. If not, they say whether the application is without notice.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Continue</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_enter_general_application", locals: { caption: "6. Upload general application", page: :upload } %><p class="bf-journey__note">They upload the N244. This file is required.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Continue</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_enter_general_application", locals: { caption: "7. Upload related evidence", page: :evidence } %><p class="bf-journey__note">Related evidence is optional. They can add documents or continue without any.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Continue</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_enter_general_application", locals: { caption: "8. Refer to judge", page: :refer } %><p class="bf-journey__note">Shown only when the parties do not consent and the application is without notice. The page tells them to refer it to a judge. It does not send the referral.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Continue</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_enter_general_application", locals: { caption: "9. Check your answers", page: :summary } %><p class="bf-journey__note">They check the answers and select <strong>Submit</strong>. The case state does not change.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Submit</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_enter_general_application", locals: { caption: "10. Application entered", page: :confirmation } %><p class="bf-journey__note">The confirmation is <strong>Application entered</strong>, with the case number and what happens next.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Case details</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_case_details", locals: { caption: "11. TEC PCN — Case details", highlight_tab: :case_details, show_general_applications: true } %><p class="bf-journey__note">Case details lists the application under <strong>General applications</strong>, including state <strong>Issued</strong>. The N244 is in Case File View <strong>Applications</strong>. Related evidence is in <strong>Uncategorised</strong>.</p></div>
</div>

## Journey: Review an out-of-time validation failure

Caseworker picks up a validation-failure task from **My work**, reviews the TE9/TE7 (or PE3/PE2) pair on Case details, compares scanned documents in Case File View, corrects OCR data via **Edit application** if needed, then completes **Validate OOT application**. **Form valid** revalidates against business rules; **Form invalid** continues to **Edit rejection email**, where they can change a draft email to the respondent. After submit they land on **History**.

<div class="bf-journey">
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_my_tasks_minimal", locals: { caption: "1. My work — My tasks", compact: true, highlight_case: true } %><p class="bf-journey__note">Caseworker selects a task relating to a case and clicks the <strong>case reference</strong> link.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Case link</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_case_details", locals: { caption: "2. TEC PCN — Case details", validation_errors: true, highlight_tab: :case_file } %><p class="bf-journey__note">They review validation errors on the out-of-time pair that should have been sent: <strong>TE9 / TE7</strong> (or <strong>PE3 / PE2</strong>).</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Case File View</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_case_file", locals: { caption: "3. TEC PCN — Case File View" } %><p class="bf-journey__note">They compare the application data with the original scanned documents.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Next steps</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_tasks", locals: { caption: "4. TEC PCN — Tasks", highlight: true, callout: true, highlight_step: :edit } %><p class="bf-journey__note">If scanned data can be corrected, they choose <strong>Edit application</strong> from Next steps for the form that needs fixing.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Edit application</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_edit_application", locals: { caption: "5. Event — Edit TE9 application" } %><p class="bf-journey__note">They edit the OCR fields for the form that failed validation, then continue.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Continue</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_case_details", locals: { caption: "6. TEC PCN — Case details" } %><p class="bf-journey__note">After saving edits they return to Case details with the updated application sections.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Next steps</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_tasks", locals: { caption: "7. TEC PCN — Tasks", highlight: true, callout: true, highlight_step: :validate } %><p class="bf-journey__note">They complete the task by selecting <strong>Validate OOT application</strong> from Next steps.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Validate</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_validate_application", locals: { caption: "8. Event — Validate (Form valid)", result: :valid } %><p class="bf-journey__note">If the form has been corrected they select <strong>Form valid</strong>. The system revalidates the data against business rules.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">or</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_validate_application", locals: { caption: "9. Event — Validate (Form invalid)", result: :invalid } %><p class="bf-journey__note">If they select <strong>Form invalid</strong> and continue, the next screen is the rejection email.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Continue</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_edit_rejection_email", locals: { caption: "10. Event — Edit rejection email" } %><p class="bf-journey__note">The page is headed <strong>Edit rejection email</strong>. The text box contains a draft to the respondent, with the GOV.UK Notify placeholder <strong>((respondent_name))</strong>, saying the application has been rejected because it is not valid.</p></div>
<div class="bf-journey__arrow"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="bf-journey__arrow-label">Submit</span></div>
<div class="bf-journey__step"><%= partial "partials/blockframe/views/tec_pcn_history", locals: { caption: "11. TEC PCN — History" } %><p class="bf-journey__note">After submitting the form the user is returned to Case history.</p></div>
</div>

